    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493310108/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """seemed very sad at going to Russia to play in French rôles, having devoted five years entirely to D’Annunzio, and very sad also that other people might now (so she has arranged with him) take up his Plays. She spoke simply and frankly about it, and I wondered if one of the reasons of her extreme seclusion (besides amourousness) might not be her tendency to speak frankly about herself, and take people into her intimacy.
Saturday, Mar. 21. 03.
At least she came over this morning and spoke without disguise about D’Annunzio, how he is overworking himself, and she asked me to arrange for more music to distract him in the evening. She spoke just """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 179 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

